      "text": "The diagonal of the square can be found using the Pythagorean theorem. Since the two sides of the square are congruent, each side is $\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}= \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. The area of the square is $\\left(\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2= \\frac{25}{2}$.\n\nThe circle's diameter is 5, so the radius is 2.5. The area of the circle is $\\pi \\cdot 2.5^2= \\frac{25\\pi}{4}$. The difference is $| \\frac{ 25}{2}- \\frac{ 25 \\pi }{4} |$ . After simplifying, the answer is less than 16.25, which is our final answer.",
