      "text": "Iook at the picture above.  The square in blue represents a square with side length $5/√2$ , the circle in teal represents a circle with radius $1.414/2$ , and the rectangle in purple represents a rectangle with side length $5$ and width $2.828/2=1.414$ .  So, I am going to find the area of each shape separately, the difference between the two areas will then be my answer.  I know that the area of the square is $5^2$ .  Since side lengths of the square are half of the diagonal, each of the sides of the square will be $5/√2$ .  The area of a square is side length by side length.  Also, each of the sides of the blue rectangle will be $1.414/2$ .  Thus the area of the rectangle is $5\\cdot 1.414/2$ .  Furthermore, I can take the area of the square, which is $5^2$ , and subtract the area of the rectangle, which is $5\\cdot 1.414/2$  My answer will be in square inches, luckily it is given to us.  \n[asy]\n /* Geogebra to Asymptote conversion, documentation at artofproblemsolving.com/Wiki, go to User:Azjps/geogebra */\nimport graph; size(12cm); \nreal labelscalefactor = 0.5; /* changes label-to-point distance */\npen dps = linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(10); defaultpen(dps); /* default pen style */ \npen dotstyle = black; /* point style */ \nreal xmin = -15.154432762327431, xmax = 15.228502425340661, ymin = -13.963358853748756, ymax = 13.364658743931682;  /* image dimensions */\n /* layer 0 */\n /* layer 1 */\n draw(circle((0.7,-1.5), 4.1), linewidth(1.)); \n draw((0,13)--(-4.3,-3.5)--(4.3,-3.5), linewidth(1));\n draw((-4.3,-3.5)--(0,-13)); \n draw(((0,13)--(-4.3,-3.5)),linewidth(1));\n draw(\"--\" (13,0) (0,13));\n draw((3,-12)--(-6,-14)--(-3,-18)--(6,-16)--(3,-12) (2,-11)--(7,-11)--(5,-13)--(7,-13)--(2,-11)); /* \"Square 1\" */\n draw((0,3)--(8.4,-4.5)); \n label(\"5\", (2.62,5.16)); \n draw((6.25,-5.7)--(2.25,-4.2)--(2.2,5)--(14,6.1)-(7,7.4)--(7,-7.8)--(10,-7.7)); /* \"Rectangle 2\" */\n draw((-4,0.7)--(14,7)--(8,-8)--(.5,-6)--(0,-4)); \n dot((-4,0.7)); \n dot((14,7));\n dot((8,-8));\n dot((.5,-6));\n dot((0,-4));\n label(\"5\", (5.3,5.5));\n dot((1.5,-4));\n dot((-0.3,-8));\n dot((-3.7,-6));\n label(\"2\", (3.3,-6.5));\n label(\"13.5\", (6.0,-3));\n label(\"6\", (6.0,-0.5));\n label(\"22.4\", (-2,-4.05));\n dot((0,13));\n draw((-4.3,-3.5)--(5,6.5));\n draw((2.5,4.5)--(-6,-5));\n dot((0.5,12)); \n dot((8,-3));\n dot((-5,-11)); \n dot((3,-12)); \n dot((-7,-13));\n dot((4,14));\n label(\"5\", (2.3,-14));\n /* layer 2 */\n  /* layer 2 */\n [/asy]\nThus, $5^2 - (5\\cdot 1.414/2) = 25 - 3.53 = \\boxed{{21.47}}$",
